	// resolved and enforced per declaring file. The underlying PRIMITIVE is not: the readers that
	// have no file to ask from -- type resolution of a struct field, union payload classification
	// reached from the emitted runtime, generic type-argument and conformance-signature
	// canonicalization -- all read it through one bare-name door, so a name whose declarations
	// disagree about int-vs-float has no answer that door can give. It is refused at the SECOND
	// file's declaration rather than answered arbitrarily.
