	// setter is bounded by CAPACITY rather than by length (a 2026-07-30 user ruling), so it can
	// write into `[length, capacity)` -- slots no length has published yet. For a TRIVIAL element
	// that is the whole point: it is the stage-then-`setLength`-to-publish idiom the buffer surface
	// exists to support. For a MANAGED element it opens a hole, because that region carries no
	// OWNERSHIP: `__managed_decref` destroys only `[0, length)`, `push`/`insert`/`append` store AT
