	// the associated type and can never name what a conformer bound it to. There is no whole-program
	// conformance registry mid-parse (`project.conformances` is filled at merge, after every file has parsed),
	// so the front end has nothing to ask.
	// MEASURED before the rule existed:
	// * `with float` -- x64-windows compiled clean and answered 35 where the program computes 31, the f64
	// read out of the integer return register, while wasm32-wasi trapped;
	// * `with String` and `with Point` -- both ran to completion and exited 101, the LEAK gate, on x64 AND
	// wasm. The same interface with the return SPELLED `String` instead of associated is clean, which
	// attributes the leak exactly to this path.
