	// and the runtime walk calls it with exactly one argument plus the uniform `__env` slot.
	// USER RULING 2026-08-04, and a DELIBERATE divergence from the reference bootstrap, which accepts the
	// shape: a transform declaring a further parameter reads a value nobody passed. MEASURED --
	// `nums.map(function(a Integer, b Integer) gives b)` prints `sum=0` on arm64-macOS, `b` being whatever
	// the second argument slot held, while on `wasm32-wasi` the program does not run at all: `call_indirect`
	// type-checks the callee's signature and `__managed_map` traps with "indirect call type mismatch". One
	// target of four could see it, which is what makes the shape undefined rather than unspecified.
	// NOT E3036, which states that "a call passes a different number of arguments than the callee declares
	// parameters": there is NO call at this span. The author bound a function VALUE to a position, and the
	// call that would go wrong is one the compiler makes inside `__managed_map`, over a source line the author
	// never wrote -- so E3036's sentence would be false about the program in front of them.
	// NOT E3005 either, which is what the four DECLARED function-typed places (a cast, a `return`, an
	// assignment, an ordinary function-typed argument) earn when their whole SHAPE disagrees. This position
